{"c":[{"name":"20261018T171639Z-5cb80849a2e584b6","text":"Nightly cron/launchd entries carry PATH and the resolved STOCKROOM_HOME (no shell profile is loaded); 'schedule status' prints up-to-date: and entry home:, and sr-initialize Step 8 offers a consented re-install of a stale entry.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261018T203924Z-9f05cc054dcdf6ff","text":"Path quoting also covers commands stockroom prints for someone to run (doctor smoke's torch remedy, localdev.sh's --plugin-dir hint). When auditing shell text, search printed messages too, not only code that runs a shell.","type":"note"}]}
